  "worked_solution": "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n2{x}_{3}=4\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}+3(2)=7\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{2}=6-7=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5(-1)+(2)=-1\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=-1+5-2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$",
